                <pb facs="0518" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/781: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nogales</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Damm</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nogales, Ariz</hi></placeName>., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-23T18:00:00-06:00">April 23, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:37 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>From Guaymas.</p>
                <p>“Urgent. April 23, 4 p.m. Please expedite reply my April 22, 1 p.m., as similar
                    case arises in connection with Standard Oil Company stocks at Yavaros, and it
                    may become necessary to request to have ordered to Yavaros destroyer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Selfridge</hi> now on the way to relieve <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Robert Smith</hi> at Guaymas.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Damm</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
